Adapted designs (no source copied)
----------------------------------

runtime/crates/tool-runtime/src/lib.rs adapts process-group reaping from OpenAI
Codex (Apache-2.0), codex-rs/utils/pty/src/process_group.rs: the child leads its
own process group, and the group rather than the single pid is signalled so a
timeout ends everything a Tool started. Codex escalates SIGTERM to SIGKILL; this
project sends SIGKILL directly. No Codex source is copied. See
docs/third-party-sources.md.

runtime/crates/tool-runtime/src/seatbelt.rs adapts the macOS Seatbelt containment
approach from OpenAI Codex (Apache-2.0), codex-rs/sandboxing: invoking
/usr/bin/sandbox-exec by absolute path, passing filesystem paths as profile
parameters rather than interpolating them, restricting reads by allowing
everything and then appending targeted deny rules (SBPL resolves by last match),
pairing subpath with literal so the directory node itself is covered, and
normalizing paths before they enter the profile because macOS symlinks /var and
/tmp into /private. The profile text and the executor integration are original to
this project. See docs/third-party-sources.md,
docs/adr/0036-seatbelt-contained-trusted-tools-and-workspace-writes.md and
docs/adr/0037-sensitive-path-read-containment.md.
